module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Generators
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.CoversTop.Over
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.OverFiniteFree
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SliceRestrictionColimits

/-!
# Descent of freeness and of generation by sections from a covering family

Let `R` be a sheaf of rings on a site `(C, J)` and `F` a sheaf of `R`-modules. This file proves
the three descent statements that remain after
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/OverFiniteFree.lean`: if a family `Y : I → C`
covers the terminal object and the restriction of `F` to every `Y i` is

* a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf indexed by an **arbitrary** type, or
* generated by global sections, or
* generated by global sections indexed by a type equivalent to `Fin r`,

then the same holds, locally on any object `W`, after restriction to a covering family of `W`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeOverMapIso`: the free sheaf of modules on `I` over the slice site at
  `Z` is the restriction along `h : Z ⟶ Y` of the free sheaf of modules on `I` over the slice site
  at `Y`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOver`: restriction along `h : Z ⟶ Y` of a family of
  generating sections of `F.over Y`, as a family of generating sections of `F.over Z` indexed by
  the *same* type.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCofanOverOfType` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_isColimitCofan_over_of_le'`: restriction along `h : Z ⟶ Y`
  carries a cofan exhibiting `F.over Y` as a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf indexed by
  a type `B` to one for `F.over Z`, with the same `B`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop`: the descent statement
  for freeness of arbitrary rank.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCofanOverOfTypeOfSheafify`,
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_isColimitCofan_over_of_le_of_sheafify` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop'`: the same three
  statements with no fibre products assumed in the site, from sheafification of the slice sites
  instead.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_cover_generatingSections_of_coversTop`: the descent statement for
  generation by global sections, in the slice-site covering form
  `(J.over W).CoversTop`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_cover_generatingSections_equiv_of_coversTop`: the descent
  statement for generation by a family of sections indexed by a fixed type `A`, in any universe —
  with `A := Fin r` this is generation by `r` sections.

## Implementation notes

**Why `[Limits.HasPullbacks C]` is present and what it buys.** All three statements rest on one
fact: restriction `SheafOfModules.overMap R h` along `h : Z ⟶ Y` preserves coproducts of copies of
the structure sheaf, and preserves epimorphisms. For a *finite* index type both follow from
additivity of `overMap` and need no hypothesis on `C` at all; that is the route taken in
`OverFiniteFree.lean`, and it is why the finite-rank statement lives there. For an arbitrary index
type additivity is not enough. Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.overMapPushforwardAdj` exhibits
`overMap R h` as a *left* adjoint — to `SheafOfModules.overPullback R h`, which is restriction
along `Over.pullback h` and therefore needs fibre products in `C` — and a left adjoint preserves
all colimits and all epimorphisms. `[Limits.HasPullbacks C]` is exactly the hypothesis under which
Mathlib states that adjunction. It is a hypothesis on the *site*, not on the sheaf of modules or
on the covering family: nothing in the statements is weakened by it, and the index types of the
free bases and of the generating families are transported unchanged.

**It is not the only hypothesis that buys that fact, and the two are incomparable.**
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.overMap_preservesColimits` proves the same preservation statement from
sheafification of the abelian sheaves on the slice sites — `HasWeakSheafify` and
`WEqualsLocallyBijective` for every `J.over X`, i.e. exactly the hypotheses the generation
statements further down this file already carry — by commuting sheafification with restriction
along the continuous cocontinuous functor `Over.map h`, with no fibre products anywhere. The
section `FreeSheafify` repeats the three freeness statements under those hypotheses instead;
`isColimitCofanOverOfTypeOfPreserves` and
`exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop_of_descent` hold the shared content, so the two
routes differ only in how the preservation fact is supplied.

**No sheafification of the slice sites beyond what `free` already needs.**
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` is defined in terms of `SheafOfModules.free` and
`SheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv`, which require `HasWeakSheafify` and `WEqualsLocallyBijective` for
`AddCommGrpCat.{w}` on the site carrying the sheaf of modules; since the sheaves of modules here
live on the slice sites `J.over X`, those instances are assumed for every `X : C` and for no other
site. In particular `freeOverMapIso` is built by hand from
`SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan` and `IsColimit.coconePointsIsoOfNatIso` rather than by
invoking `SheafOfModules.mapFreeIso`, whose section in Mathlib carries the strictly stronger
`HasSheafify` on the target site. The isomorphism produced is the same one.

**Universes.** The index type `I` of the covering family is free. The index type of a free basis
and of a family of generating sections must live in the universe `w` of the sections of the sheaf
of rings: `SheafOfModules.unit R` and `SheafOfModules.free I` only typecheck there. The covering
family produced on an object `W` is indexed by a subtype of `Over W`, hence lives in
`Type (max u v)`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL) — the definitions of free,
  locally free, and locally generated sheaves of modules on a ringed site.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DN) — the statement that these
  conditions may be checked on the members of a covering family. This file proves the descent
  direction and carries no tag of its own.
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits

universe t a w v u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-! ### Freeness of arbitrary rank -/

/-- Restriction along `h : Z ⟶ Y` of a cofan exhibiting `F.over Y` as a coproduct of copies of the
structure sheaf indexed by a type `B`, as a cofan exhibiting `F.over Z` as a coproduct of copies of
the structure sheaf indexed by the same `B`.

Takes the one fact it uses — that restriction carries the coproduct of `B` copies of the structure
sheaf to a coproduct — as an explicit argument, because two unrelated hypotheses supply it: fibre
products in the site, through the adjunction of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCofanOverOfType`,
and sheafification of the slice sites, through
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCofanOverOfTypeOfSheafify`. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCofanOverOfTypeOfPreserves
    (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) {Z Y : C} (h : Z ⟶ Y) {B : Type w}
    (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Y) ⟶ F.over Y))
    (hp : PreservesColimit (Discrete.functor fun _ : B => SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Y))
      (SheafOfModules.overMap.{w} R h))
    (hc : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Y) ι)) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Z)
      (fun j => (SheafOfModules.overMap R h).map (ι j) ≫
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctorMap R h).app F).hom)) := by
  letI := hp
  refine IsColimit.ofIsoColimit
    (isColimitOfPreserves (SheafOfModules.overMap.{w} R h) hc)
    (Cocone.ext ((SheafOfModules.overFunctorMap R h).app F) ?_)
  rintro ⟨j⟩
  rfl

/-- If a family of objects `Y` covers the terminal object and freeness of arbitrary rank descends
along every arrow of the site, then every object `W` carries a covering family of arrows on whose
sources the restriction of `F` is a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf.

The descent hypothesis is the only input; the two hypotheses on the site under which it is
available are those of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop` and
of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop'`. -/
theorem exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop_of_descent
    {I : Type t} (Y : I → C) (hY : J.CoversTop Y) (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (hdesc : ∀ {Z Y' : C} (_h : Z ⟶ Y'),
      (∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Y') ⟶ F.over Y')),
        Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Y') ι))) →
      ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Z) ⟶ F.over Z)),
        Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Z) ι)))
    (hF : ∀ i, ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over (Y i)) ⟶ F.over (Y i))),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over (Y i)) ι)))
    (W : C) :
    ∃ (I' : Type (max u v)) (V : I' → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ W),
      Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J W ∧
        ∀ i, ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over (V i)) ⟶ F.over (V i))),
          Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over (V i)) ι)) := by
  refine ⟨Σ Z : C, { g : Z ⟶ W // (Sieve.ofObjects Y W).arrows g }, fun x => x.1,
    fun x => x.2.1, ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine J.superset_covering ?_ (hY W)
    intro Z g hg
    exact Sieve.ofArrows_mk _ _ (⟨Z, g, hg⟩ : Σ Z : C, { g : Z ⟶ W // _ })
  · rintro ⟨Z, g, i, ⟨h⟩⟩
    exact hdesc h (hF i)

section Free

variable [HasPullbacks C]

/-- Restriction along `h : Z ⟶ Y` of a cofan exhibiting `F.over Y` as a coproduct of copies of the
structure sheaf indexed by a type `B`, as a cofan exhibiting `F.over Z` as a coproduct of copies of
the structure sheaf indexed by the same `B`.

Unlike `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCofanOver`, which covers the case `B = Fin n` by additivity
of restriction, this uses that restriction is a left adjoint and hence needs fibre products in the
site. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCofanOverOfType
    (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) {Z Y : C} (h : Z ⟶ Y) {B : Type w}
    (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Y) ⟶ F.over Y))
    (hc : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Y) ι)) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Z)
      (fun j => (SheafOfModules.overMap R h).map (ι j) ≫
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctorMap R h).app F).hom)) :=
  isColimitCofanOverOfTypeOfPreserves F h ι inferInstance hc

/-- Freeness of arbitrary rank of a sheaf of modules on a slice site is inherited by every smaller
slice site, with the same index type. -/
theorem exists_isColimitCofan_over_of_le'
    (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) {Z Y : C} (h : Z ⟶ Y)
    (hF : ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Y) ⟶ F.over Y)),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Y) ι))) :
    ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Z) ⟶ F.over Z)),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Z) ι)) := by
  obtain ⟨B, ι, ⟨hc⟩⟩ := hF
  exact ⟨B, _, ⟨isColimitCofanOverOfType F h ι hc⟩⟩

/-- If a family of objects `Y` covers the terminal object and the restriction of `F` to each `Y i`
is a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf, then every object `W` carries a covering family of
arrows on whose sources the same holds. This is the covering-family criterion for local freeness of
arbitrary rank. -/
theorem exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop
    {I : Type t} (Y : I → C) (hY : J.CoversTop Y) (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (hF : ∀ i, ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over (Y i)) ⟶ F.over (Y i))),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over (Y i)) ι)))
    (W : C) :
    ∃ (I' : Type (max u v)) (V : I' → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ W),
      Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J W ∧
        ∀ i, ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over (V i)) ⟶ F.over (V i))),
          Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over (V i)) ι)) :=
  exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop_of_descent Y hY F
    (fun h => exists_isColimitCofan_over_of_le' F h) hF W

end Free

/-! ### Freeness of arbitrary rank, through sheafification of the slice sites

The same three statements under a hypothesis on the site **incomparable** to `[HasPullbacks C]`:
sheafification, in the weak form, of the abelian sheaves on every slice site, which is what
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.overMap_preservesColimits` needs. The two routes to "restriction preserves
coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf" are genuinely different — an adjunction built from
fibre products in one case, the commutation of sheafification with restriction along a continuous
cocontinuous functor in the other — so neither statement subsumes the other, and this section
exists because the hypotheses below are exactly the ones already needed for generation by sections
further down this file. -/

section FreeSheafify

variable [∀ X : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- Restriction along `h : Z ⟶ Y` of a cofan exhibiting `F.over Y` as a coproduct of copies of the
structure sheaf indexed by a type `B`, as a cofan exhibiting `F.over Z` as a coproduct of copies of
the structure sheaf indexed by the same `B`.  Needs no fibre products in the site. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCofanOverOfTypeOfSheafify
    (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) {Z Y : C} (h : Z ⟶ Y) {B : Type w}
    (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Y) ⟶ F.over Y))
    (hc : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Y) ι)) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Z)
      (fun j => (SheafOfModules.overMap R h).map (ι j) ≫
        ((SheafOfModules.overFunctorMap R h).app F).hom)) :=
  letI : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w} (SheafOfModules.overMap.{w} R h) :=
    overMap_preservesColimits R h
  isColimitCofanOverOfTypeOfPreserves F h ι inferInstance hc

/-- Freeness of arbitrary rank of a sheaf of modules on a slice site is inherited by every smaller
slice site, with the same index type.  Needs no fibre products in the site. -/
theorem exists_isColimitCofan_over_of_le_of_sheafify
    (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) {Z Y : C} (h : Z ⟶ Y)
    (hF : ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Y) ⟶ F.over Y)),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Y) ι))) :
    ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over Z) ⟶ F.over Z)),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over Z) ι)) := by
  obtain ⟨B, ι, ⟨hc⟩⟩ := hF
  exact ⟨B, _, ⟨isColimitCofanOverOfTypeOfSheafify F h ι hc⟩⟩

/-- The covering-family criterion for local freeness of arbitrary rank, with no fibre products
assumed in the site. -/
theorem exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop'
    {I : Type t} (Y : I → C) (hY : J.CoversTop Y) (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (hF : ∀ i, ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over (Y i)) ⟶ F.over (Y i))),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over (Y i)) ι)))
    (W : C) :
    ∃ (I' : Type (max u v)) (V : I' → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ W),
      Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J W ∧
        ∀ i, ∃ (B : Type w) (ι : B → (SheafOfModules.unit (R.over (V i)) ⟶ F.over (V i))),
          Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over (V i)) ι)) :=
  exists_cover_isColimitCofanOfType_of_coversTop_of_descent Y hY F
    (fun h => exists_isColimitCofan_over_of_le_of_sheafify F h) hF W

end FreeSheafify

/-! ### Generation by global sections -/

section Generators

variable [∀ X : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasPullbacks C]

/-- The free sheaf of modules on `A` over the slice site at `Z` is the restriction along
`h : Z ⟶ Y` of the free sheaf of modules on `A` over the slice site at `Y`.

This is `SheafOfModules.mapFreeIso` for the functor `SheafOfModules.overMap R h`, written out so as
not to require `HasSheafify` on the slice site at `Z`: `SheafOfModules.free` itself needs only
`HasWeakSheafify`, and the comparison isomorphism is the universal one between two colimit cocones
over isomorphic diagrams. -/
noncomputable def freeOverMapIso {Z Y : C} (h : Z ⟶ Y) (A : Type w) :
    SheafOfModules.free (R := R.over Z) A ≅
      (SheafOfModules.overMap R h).obj (SheafOfModules.free (R := R.over Y) A) :=
  (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan A).coconePointsIsoOfNatIso
    (isColimitOfPreserves (SheafOfModules.overMap.{w} R h) (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan A))
    (Discrete.natIso fun _ => (SheafOfModules.overMapUnitIso (R := R) h).symm)

/-- Restriction along `h : Z ⟶ Y` of a family of generating sections of `F.over Y`, as a family of
generating sections of `F.over Z`.

The index type is unchanged: by construction `(generatingSectionsOver F h σ).I = σ.I`. The
epimorphism `free σ.I ⟶ F.over Z` is the image of `σ.π` under restriction, read through
`freeOverMapIso` and `SheafOfModules.overFunctorMap`; it is an epimorphism because restriction is a
left adjoint. -/
noncomputable def generatingSectionsOver (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) {Z Y : C} (h : Z ⟶ Y)
    (σ : (F.over Y).GeneratingSections) : (F.over Z).GeneratingSections where
  I := σ.I
  s := (F.over Z).freeHomEquiv ((freeOverMapIso h σ.I).hom ≫
    (SheafOfModules.overMap R h).map σ.π ≫ ((SheafOfModules.overFunctorMap R h).app F).hom)
  epi := by
    rw [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
    have : Epi ((SheafOfModules.overMap.{w} R h).map σ.π) :=
      Functor.map_epi (SheafOfModules.overMap.{w} R h) σ.π
    infer_instance

/-- The restricted family `generatingSectionsOver F h σ` has the same index type as `σ`. -/
@[simp]
lemma generatingSectionsOver_I (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) {Z Y : C} (h : Z ⟶ Y)
    (σ : (F.over Y).GeneratingSections) : (generatingSectionsOver F h σ).I = σ.I := rfl

/-- If a family of objects `Y` covers the terminal object and the restriction of `F` to each `Y i`
is generated by global sections, then for every object `W` there is a family of objects of
`Over W` covering the terminal object of the slice site at `W` on whose sources the restriction of
`F` is again generated by global sections. -/
theorem exists_cover_generatingSections_of_coversTop
    {I : Type t} (Y : I → C) (hY : J.CoversTop Y) (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (hF : ∀ i, Nonempty ((F.over (Y i)).GeneratingSections)) (W : C) :
    ∃ (I' : Type (max u v)) (V : I' → Over W), (J.over W).CoversTop V ∧
      ∀ i, Nonempty ((F.over (V i).left).GeneratingSections) := by
  refine ⟨{ Z : Over W // Nonempty ((F.over Z.left).GeneratingSections) }, Subtype.val,
    ?_, fun i => i.2⟩
  intro T
  refine (J.over W).superset_covering ?_
    ((Over.forget W).cover_lift (J.over W) J (hY T.left))
  intro Z g hg
  obtain ⟨i, ⟨h⟩⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ ((Over.forget W).map g)).1 hg
  exact (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ g).2
    ⟨⟨Z, ⟨generatingSectionsOver F h (hF i).some⟩⟩, ⟨𝟙 Z⟩⟩

/-- If a family of objects `Y` covers the terminal object and the restriction of `F` to each `Y i`
is generated by a family of global sections indexed by a type equivalent to `A`, then every object
`W` has a covering sieve all of whose arrows have the same property at their source.

With `A := Fin r` this is descent of "locally generated by `r` sections". -/
theorem exists_cover_generatingSections_equiv_of_coversTop (A : Type a)
    {I : Type t} (Y : I → C) (hY : J.CoversTop Y) (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (hF : ∀ i, ∃ σ : (F.over (Y i)).GeneratingSections, Nonempty (σ.I ≃ A)) (W : C) :
    ∃ S : J.Cover W, ∀ (V : C) (f : V ⟶ W), S f →
      ∃ σ : (F.over V).GeneratingSections, Nonempty (σ.I ≃ A) := by
  refine ⟨hY.cover W, fun V f hf => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨i, ⟨h⟩⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ f).1 hf
  obtain ⟨σ, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hF i
  exact ⟨generatingSectionsOver F h σ, ⟨e⟩⟩

end Generators

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
